    "answer": {
      "state": "completed",
      "text": "Outcome: resolve_funding. The manuscript is not ready for PLOS submission because no funding statement has been entered (ref-441cfc1d3f0a9431c3c39754). PLOS requires a funding statement, and that requirement applies even when no funding was received.\n\nThe other checks pass on the gathered evidence:\n- **Exclusivity:** the work exists only as a preprint and is not under consideration at another journal (ref-a5abd1c00445ee8f78ae47f4).\n- **Author approval:** every listed author has approved the submitted version (ref-d7dcf9cd838ef340322f6476).\n- **Data:** the data and metadata are in a named repository, and the data statement gives the persistent identifier (ref-e062fdbbbda475e7a404b072).\n- **Competing interests:** all relevant potential competing interests are disclosed (ref-a9b8b059e0293be74129f52a).\n- **Code:** no analysis relied on code the authors wrote themselves (ref-718c6f3222570a7dec0d2352).\n\nThe recruiting community group has asked for an extra community data-sharing review before publication (ref-e062fdbbbda475e7a404b072). That is an outside commitment, not a PLOS data-availability gap, so it does not change the outcome. Still, the team should keep track of it.\n\nNext step: Fatima Meyer (Grants Administrator) and Sanjay Singh should supply the funding statement. This would be either the grant and funder details or an explicit statement that no funding was received. The readiness review can then be re-run.",
      "used_evidence_refs": [
        "ref-441cfc1d3f0a9431c3c39754",
        "ref-a5abd1c00445ee8f78ae47f4",
